<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Judah</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Judah was an ancient kingdom in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. It was conquered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaldean-empire">Chaldean Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii">Nebuchadnezzar II</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportations</a> of its people to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> in 597 and 587 BCE supplied skilled labour to the Chaldean economy and began the Babylonian exile.</p></div>
